724
00:56:34,096 --> 00:56:37,845
and then the way Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) built it and then again on the foundations of Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم).

725
00:56:38,167 --> 00:56:40,332
Imam Malik(امام مالك) said that,

726
00:56:40,362 --> 00:56:44,440
the people have known Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) and they have known these stones the way they are,

727
00:56:44,906 --> 00:56:48,148
don't keep on changing it, keep it the way it is.

728
00:56:48,714 --> 00:56:53,831
And that was a very wise advice from Al-Imam Malik(الامام مالك) which the Khalifah(خليفه) followed.

729
00:56:54,573 --> 00:56:58,910
So, the Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) that we have today is built on which foundation,

730
00:56:59,000 --> 00:57:02,431
the foundation of Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) or the foundations of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ)?

731
00:57:03,138 --> 00:57:03,879
Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

732
00:57:04,333 --> 00:57:06,236
But Al-Hamdolillah(الحمدلله) that's something good.

733
00:57:07,155 --> 00:57:08,035
Why.?

734
00:57:09,009 --> 00:57:13,142
If Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) was built on the original foundations of Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم),

735
00:57:14,268 --> 00:57:18,040
we would have been deprived the chance of praying inside Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه).

736
00:57:19,304 --> 00:57:20,930
But since it is shortened.

737
00:57:21,947 --> 00:57:27,164
That area which is enclosedby the semi circle is actually part of Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه).

738
00:57:27,396 --> 00:57:33,402
So, when you pray in that area, it is as if you have prayed inside Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه).

739
00:57:35,008 --> 00:57:37,933
And we know that Rasool Allah ﷺ did pray inside Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه).

740
00:57:38,665 --> 00:57:41,195
When he opened Makkah, he prayed inside Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه),

741
00:57:41,410 --> 00:57:43,896
he prayed eight Rak'ah(ركعة) inside Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه).

742
00:57:44,120 --> 00:57:46,869
So, now we have a chance to pray in Al-Hijr(الحجر).

743
00:57:48,724 --> 00:57:51,491
Otherwise, we would have to get permission to get inside Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه)

744
00:57:51,516 --> 00:57:54,046
and it would be very cumbersome and difficult.

745
00:57:54,867 --> 00:58:01,092
But now we can pray inside Al-Hijr(الحجر) and it will count as if you prayed in Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه).

746
00:58:02,777 --> 00:58:10,155
Now over the time, the height of Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) has increased, but the size of it has remained constant.

747
00:58:11,087 --> 00:58:15,238
Now, with the stones that Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه), are built from,

748
00:58:15,561 --> 00:58:22,223
many of them are remnants of the original stones that were used by Ibrahim عليه السّلام,

749
00:58:22,464 --> 00:58:27,430
but not all of them. Some other ones were introduced later by Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) and others.

750
00:58:27,904 --> 00:58:34,244
But the black stone is the original stone that was used by Ibrahim عليه السّلام.

751
00:58:34,345 --> 00:58:41,726
The black stone has never changed, it is the original stone that was given to Ibrahim عليه السّلام.

752
00:58:42,015 --> 00:58:45,010
And there are many stories about the black stone itself.

753
00:58:45,349 --> 00:58:49,710
Some say it originated from Jannah(جنة), there's a Hadith(حديث) that is authentic that says that

754
00:58:49,760 --> 00:58:55,080
 the black stone was white, but then it turned black because of the sins of the sons of Adam(آدم).

755
00:58:55,833 --> 00:59:01,497
And there is a Hadith(حديث) that says that the black stone is right hand of Allah on Earth.

756
00:59:02,094 --> 00:59:05,716
So, the black stone is very special, it's very honored,

757
00:59:06,216 --> 00:59:12,008
and it's very respected and it's the only part of Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) that is kissed

758
00:59:12,962 --> 00:59:16,995
and is only part of Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) that is pointed to from a distance.

759
00:59:17,020 --> 00:59:20,701
Some people they point to the Yemeni corner which is wrong

760
00:59:20,726 --> 00:59:24,091
and Yemeni corner you can touch it when you're passing by it.

761
00:59:24,574 --> 00:59:30,251
But one should not point towards it, or greet it from a distance that is only for the black stone.

762
00:59:30,738 --> 00:59:33,970
So, this is the history of Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه).

763
00:59:35,377 --> 00:59:49,271
The Prophet ﷺ would go out of Makkah and spend time in the cave of Hira(حرا)

764
00:59:51,018 --> 00:59:57,035
in a mountain that is fairly close to Makkah a few kilometers away from Makkah.

765
00:59:58,040 --> 01:00:02,269
Rasool Allah ﷺ will take with him provisions, some food

766
01:00:02,649 --> 01:00:11,370
and he would go and stay in seclusion, solitude in this cave, worshiping Allah سبحانه وتعالى,

767
01:00:12,142 --> 01:00:20,072
and from the cave it is said that you are able to see Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه), in those old days.

768
01:00:20,475 --> 01:00:28,915
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ would spend days and nights continuously in the cave, worshipping Allah سبحانه وتعالى before Prophet hood.

769
01:00:30,472 --> 01:00:35,715
So, he knew Allah سبحانه وتعالى and he was worshipping Allah سبحانه وتعالى in that cave.

770
01:00:36,611 --> 01:00:44,034
And this was a chance for Rasool Allah ﷺ to do reflectionand contemplation in the creation of Allah.

771
01:00:44,896 --> 01:00:49,210
And this was training for him Allahسبحانه وتعالى was training him

772
01:00:49,779 --> 01:00:54,406
through these moments of reflection and contemplation, because they purify the heart.

773
01:00:55,355 --> 01:00:58,597
And Saeed Hawwa(سعيد هوّا), he comments on this, he says:

774
01:00:59,007 --> 01:01:05,899
Solitude was the tradition of some, who seek the guidance of Allah, with the remembrance of Allah and worship.

775
01:01:06,527 --> 01:01:15,866
It was used to illuminate the hearts and remove its Shadows by disconnecting it from its heedlessness and desires.

776
01:01:16,254 --> 01:01:19,642
Some would advise this in the beginning of the journey to belief,

777
01:01:20,177 --> 01:01:23,284
as this was the example of the Prophet ﷺ,

778
01:01:23,342 --> 01:01:27,406
when he spent time in solitude before and at the beginning of his apostleship.

779
01:01:28,206 --> 01:01:32,655
So, as a Muslim, you are recommended to spend time alone in Zikr(زكر),

780
01:01:34,118 --> 01:01:40,531
for example, early in the morning, after Asr(عصر), between Asr(عصر) and Maghrib(مغرب) on Friday.

781
01:01:41,195 --> 01:01:43,832
So, you spend time alone remembering Allah in solitude.

782
01:01:44,623 --> 01:01:47,328
And our scholars talked about the benefit of solitude.

783
01:01:47,777 --> 01:01:55,677
Now, one should not go into the extremes of leaving the society completely,

784
01:01:56,404 --> 01:02:01,767
or immersing oneself in the society completely, it should have a middle road.

785
01:02:02,425 --> 01:02:05,433
So, you spend some time with people socializing,

786
01:02:05,715 --> 01:02:08,685
but you also spend time alone between you and Allah.

787
01:02:09,813 --> 01:02:12,533
Qiyaam Ul Lail(قيام اليل) is a chance for solitude,

788
01:02:13,065 --> 01:02:16,141
praying at night alone when everybody's asleep.

789
01:02:16,446 --> 01:02:20,472
So, it's something between you and Allah, there's an element of sincerity there,

790
01:02:20,863 --> 01:02:24,882
that might not exist with other Ibadaat(عبادات) that are done collectively.

791
01:02:25,638 --> 01:02:29,200
So now, you are doing this alone, nobody can see you, you are not showing off,

792
01:02:29,365 --> 01:02:30,440
who are you doing it for?

793
01:02:30,699 --> 01:02:31,623
You are doing it for Allah.

794
01:02:32,200 --> 01:02:38,363
So, it's very important for one, to spend this time in solitude to purify the heart.

795
01:02:38,910 --> 01:02:44,300
Because the scholars say that too much socialization, too much laughing,

796
01:02:44,935 --> 01:02:50,638
too much attachment to Duniyah(دُنِيَّا), obscures the heart and throws veils on it.

797
01:02:51,898 --> 01:02:58,612
And the way to purify the heart is by spending some time worshipping Allah سبحانه وتعالى in solitude.

798
01:02:59,541 --> 01:03:01,351
And Allah سبحانه وتعالى says about Taffakkur(تفكر):

799
01:03:01,878 --> 01:03:13,177
إِنَّ فِي خَلْقِ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضِ وَاخْتِلَافِ اللَّيْلِ وَالنَّهَارِ لَآيَاتٍ لِأُولِي الْأَلْبَابِ۝

800
01:03:13,851 --> 01:03:21,380
الَّذِينَ يَذْكُرُونَ اللَّهَ قِيَامًا وَقُعُودًا وَعَلَىٰ جُنُوبِهِمْ

801
01:03:21,712 --> 01:03:28,197
وَعَلَىٰ جُنُوبِهِمْ وَيَتَفَكَّرُونَ فِي خَلْقِ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضِ

802
01:03:28,615 --> 01:03:37,249
رَبَّنَا مَا خَلَقْتَ هَٰذَا بَاطِلًا سُبْحَانَكَ فَقِنَا عَذَابَ النَّارِ۝

803
01:03:37,767 --> 01:03:43,454
Behold, in the creation of the heavens and the earth, and the alternation of night and day,

804
01:03:43,861 --> 01:03:47,492
there are indeed signs for men of understanding.

805
01:03:47,904 --> 01:03:54,612
Men who celebrate the praises of Allah standing, sitting and laying down or lying down on their sides,

806
01:03:54,986 --> 01:04:01,681
 and contemplate the wonders of creation in the heavens and the earth with the thought,

807
01:04:01,981 --> 01:04:06,644
 Our Lord, not for not has though created all this.

808
01:04:07,048 --> 01:04:12,167
Glory to You, give us salvation from the chastisement of the fire.

809
01:04:13,060 --> 01:04:15,443
So, Allah سبحانه وتعالى is saying here that His servants

810
01:04:15,863 --> 01:04:18,841
contemplate in the creation of the heavens and earth.

811
01:04:19,749 --> 01:04:22,083
And they say: O Allah no, You have not created this in vain.

812
01:04:22,494 --> 01:04:25,646
There's purpose in creation, there's wisdom in everything that exist.

813
01:04:27,660 --> 01:04:32,032
صَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرًا

